  33:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * @fn void v_Update_Focus_State(Context_t*, Event_t*)
  34:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * @brief Respond to and event.
  35:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * The handler has two parts: immediate and non-immediate. Immediate corresponds to
  36:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * events which must be handled irrespective of what state the focus state machine is in.
  37:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * An example would be a reset or a fault. Non-immediate calls the handler for the current
  38:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * state with the event and if necessary causes the transition to a new state. If the state
  39:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * machine transitions to a new state, the exit method for the current state is called, then
  40:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * the entrance method for the new state.
  41:../src/focus_sm.c ****  *
  42:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * @param p_context Focus state context
  43:../src/focus_sm.c ****  * @param p_event Pointer to event
  44:../src/focus_sm.c ****  */
